    verification e1CryptoCoreReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "f9b68773-450a-48e7-9938-5b2a0ed2001c"; :>> title = "Sprint 1 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-11-10"; :>> createdBy = "ai"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Three review passes for Sprint 1. (1) A code review of client/src/e2ee against D0099 to D0101. (2) A crypto-mechanism review against spec sections 4.1, 4.2 and 4.4: AAD layouts, the outcome table, the pad and IV checks, the HKDF salts. (3) A clause-by-clause check of the DoD against the tests. Every finding becomes a fix in this sprint or a tracked Issue before closeOut."; }
    // RAN: Review gate for Sprint 1 (E1 e2eeCryptoCore), three passes per D0172, inspected 2026-11-10 at 904fba4. The fixes are in the closing commit. Pass 1 was a code review of client/src/e2ee and its tests by an independent reviewer: 11 findings, 1 Medium and 10 Low. Pass 2 was a crypto-mechanism review against spec sections 4.1 to 4.4 by a second independent reviewer: 7 findings, 1 Medium and 6 Low. That reviewer rebuilt the whole committed vector with node:crypto only and reproduced every value byte for byte. Pass 3 was the author's clause-by-clause check of the e2eeCryptoCore DoD against the tests: 1 finding. The shared Medium: the test titled 'a bad pad' built no bad-pad frame. So the pad check and the IV recomputation of decodeChunk had no test. Fixed with two forged frames that carry a valid tag, one with pad byte 31 set and one under a foreign IV. Both are refused, and a control reproduces the encoder frame. The wrap pad check of openKeyring got the same forged test. A decrypt spy proves no unwrap runs on a wrong password. The Lows, all fixed in the closing commit. The noble maxmem backstop is now the ceiling in u32 words. A cost above u32 or a non-integer lands in the unsupported cell, never corrupt. The create path zeroes the wrap body and every key in a finally block. openKeyring and decodeChunk return a copy, never a view over the pad. The unsupported message no longer carries its prefix twice. More Lows, also fixed. fromB64 refuses non-canonical base64. Tests cover a foreign alg and the 8 KiB per lane floor. The vector gained a precomposed non-ASCII password and three more tampered cells, eight in all. The Rust fixture test normalises CRLF before the drift compare. A try-catch test that could not fail became toThrow. One finding is the owner's call: password normalisation before the KDF. E1 feeds the raw UTF-8 as typed, the spec says so now, and it is open point 4 of spec section 8. After the fixes: 20 tests in client/test/e2ee green, tsc clean, build clean, cargo test green. Verdict PASS.
    part e1CryptoCoreReviewGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "e0148a65-2be2-4743-922e-68e8a04e9ce9"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::proposed; :>> judgedAgainst = "904fba4"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-11-10"; :>> judgedBy = "ai"; }
