    // RAN: Autonomous retro for Sprint 1 (E1 e2eeCryptoCore), analysed 2026-11-10. What the panel-fixed DoD got right: nine clauses with named functions and named outcomes made the RED suite mechanical. The outcome table and the AAD layout gave the two reviewers a byte-level contract, and one reviewer checked it with node:crypto alone. What the implementation changed: nothing in the construction. It added bytes.ts with a strict canonical base64, a copy instead of a view for VK and pt, and a test-only constructor for fixed entropy. A lint test keeps that constructor out of src. Avoidable issue: a test title promised a bad-pad case that the test never built, and both reviewers caught it. The class is a test that names a branch it does not reach. The guard that exists is the review gate itself, and it worked. A second avoidable issue: noble maxmem is a count of u32 words, and the first write used bytes. The class is a unit error in a library backstop, caught by reading the library source in review. No new item: every finding was fixed in the closing commit. The one owner fork, password normalisation, is spec section 8 point 4, beside the KDF default already tracked under d0112. Wall time: refine at 12:58, closing commit near 13:50, about one hour against the one-day guideline for 5 points. Verdict PASS.
